%description:

Tcp.fastopenCookieBytes:invalid -- an odd length stops the run with an error.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "an even number from 4 to 16".

The classes: linux (8, the default, the cookie of Linux), long (above 8: the cookie continues
with a second MAC), invalid (an odd number, below 4, above 16). The code:
Tcp::generateFastOpenCookie() makes the cookie; TcpConnection::configureStateVariables() checks
the value.

Host under test: host2. Observation: the error, and the exit code of the run.

%# parameter: Tcp.fastopenCookieBytes
%# class: invalid
%# value: 5
%# key: *.host2.tcp.fastopenCookieBytes
%# expected-result: PASS

%activity:
EV << "TcpFastopenCookieBytesInvalid compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host2.tcp.fastopenCookieBytes = 5    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%exitcode: 1

%contains-regex: stderr
fastopenCookieBytes must be an even number from 4 to 16 \(RFC 7413 section 4.1.1\), but it is 5
